.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt DF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm df
.Nd report file system disk space usage
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm df
.Op Fl ahHiklPT
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Fl x Ar type
.Op Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns Ar SIZE
.Op Fl Fl total
.Op Fl Fl output Ns Op = Ns Ar FIELD_LIST
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility displays the amount of disk space available on the file
system containing each
.Ar file
argument.
With no arguments, disk space is shown for all currently mounted
file systems.
.Pp
Values are displayed in 1K-blocks by default.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl Fl all
Include pseudo, duplicate, and inaccessible file systems in the
output.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl human-readable
Print sizes in powers of 1024 (e.g., 1023M).
.It Fl H , Fl Fl si
Print sizes in powers of 1000 (e.g., 1.1G).
.It Fl i , Fl Fl inodes
List inode information instead of block usage.
.It Fl k
Like
.Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns 1K .
.It Fl l , Fl Fl local
Limit listing to local file systems.
.It Fl P , Fl Fl portability
Use the POSIX output format (one line per filesystem).
.It Fl T , Fl Fl print-type
Print file system type.
.It Fl t Ar type , Fl Fl type Ns = Ns Ar type
Limit listing to file systems of the specified
.Ar type .
.It Fl x Ar type , Fl Fl exclude-type Ns = Ns Ar type
Exclude file systems of the specified
.Ar type .
.It Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns Ar SIZE
Scale sizes by
.Ar SIZE
before printing them.
Accepted suffixes: K, M, G, T (powers of 1024).
.It Fl Fl total
Produce a grand total line.
.It Fl Fl output Ns Op = Ns Ar FIELD_LIST
Use the output format defined by
.Ar FIELD_LIST .
Valid fields: source, fstype, size, used, avail, pcent, target.
If no
.Ar FIELD_LIST
is specified, all fields are shown.
.It Fl Fl help
Display a help message and exit.
.It Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std df
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show disk usage for all mounted file systems:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ df
Filesystem     1K-blocks      Used Available Use% Mounted on
/dev/disk1s1  488245288 234567890 253677398  48% /
.Ed
.Pp
Show disk usage in human-readable format:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ df -h
Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on
/dev/disk1s1    466G  224G  242G  48% /
.Ed
.Pp
Show file system types:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ df -T /
Filesystem     Type  1K-blocks      Used Available Use% Mounted on
/dev/disk1s1   apfs 488245288 234567890 253677398  48% /
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr du 1 ,
.Xr stat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is specified by
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
The behavior is compatible with GNU coreutils.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
